The error log indicates a `*** buffer overflow detected ***: terminated` during the execution of the `test_details` test case.

Upon inspecting the `tests/subsys/mgmt/mcumgr/enum_mgmt/src/main.c` file, the `struct details_entries` is defined with a `char expected_name[4]` field:

```c
struct details_entries {
	char expected_name[4];
	uint8_t expected_handlers;
	bool expected_test;

	bool matched_name;
	bool matched_handlers;
	bool matched_test;
};
```

In the `test_details` function, this field is initialized using `strcpy`:

```c
	strcpy(details_response[FOUND_INDEX_ENUM].expected_name, ENUM_MGMT_NAME);
```

`ENUM_MGMT_NAME` is defined as `"enum mgmt"`, which is 9 characters long plus a null terminator, requiring a buffer of at least 10 bytes. However, `expected_name` is only 4 bytes long. This results in a buffer overflow when `strcpy` attempts to write 10 bytes into a 4-byte buffer.

To fix this, the `expected_name` field needs to be large enough to accommodate the longest possible group name string, including the null terminator. The longest group name defined in this file is `SHELL_MGMT_NAME` ("shell mgmt"), which is 10 characters long. Therefore, a buffer of at least 11 bytes is required. Increasing the size to 16 bytes provides a safe margin and common alignment.

